36. Replace NULL Values With Previous Non-NULL Value

PySpark:

from pyspark.sql.functions import last
from pyspark.sql.window import Window

w = Window.orderBy("id") \
.rowsBetween(
Window.unboundedPreceding,
0
)

df.withColumn(
"filled_value",
last(
"value",
ignorenulls=True
).over(w)
)

SQL:

SELECT *,
LAST_VALUE(value)
IGNORE NULLS
OVER(
ORDER BY id
ROWS BETWEEN
UNBOUNDED PRECEDING
AND CURRENT ROW
)
FROM table_name;
